# The projects that get a repo retro every week, one per tracker, on the repo-retros timer in
# ./timers.nix, which counts its start timeout from them on the next switch; `workflow-retro --help`
# says how it is read. A retro reads every repo its project's tracker plans, so a repo planned from
# another project's tracker (quartz, from the dotfiles') has no line of its own. A second path on a
# line is the Claude Code profile the retro runs on.
~/.dotfiles
~/repos/code/yapit-tts/yapit
~/work/helferline ~/.claude-helferline
